                                "sense_id": "6b3fcf1c-99df-329b-8b0a-9da0c92da30c",
                                "text": "1741, Conny Keyber (pseudonym; attributed to Henry Fielding), An Apology for the Life of Mrs. Shamela Andrews, edited by Sheridan W. Baker, Jr., Berkeley: University of California Press, 1953, Letter 6, p. 27,\nI no sooner see him, but I scream out to Mrs. Jervis, she feigns likewise but just to come to herself; we both begin, she to becall, and I to bescratch very liberally."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "42af3a4c-ed37-4629-986d-d7ec98b5488f",
                                "sense_id": "6b3fcf1c-99df-329b-8b0a-9da0c92da30c",
                                "text": "You must not becall me for laughing when you spoke; you mistook when you thought I laughed at you as a foolish man."
                            }
